// The self-hosted form of the data-provider stdlib. A datasource ships as a Tao declaration that
// states its configuration contract and binds behavior through the published provider protocol.
// A TanStack-style cache or a remote sync engine is this same file with a different fence.

public datasource Memory {
   // Memory declares no configuration properties: a bare `Datasource Memory` instantiates it.
   // A configurable provider declares ordinary capitalized properties here, e.g.
   // `StorageKey text` (Local) or `AppId text` with defaults — validated declaratively.

   // TR.DataProvider contract (conformance suite: TR.testProvider):
   // - load() returns one starting snapshot (or empty) per app mount
   // - persist(change) is told about each committed change, in order; a rejection surfaces as
   //   provider error status and never silently drops the write
   // - status() reports loading | ready | error "message" and notifies on transition
   // The provider boundary stays deliberately narrow: queries, identity, defaults, cascade, and
   // reactivity are Tao-runtime-owned, so every provider behaves identically and stays small.
   implement inject provider ```ts
      // TODO(implementer): port the memory provider onto the TR.DataProvider protocol and return it.
      return TR.DataProvider.todo('Memory')
   ```
}
